about_text = """PRE MODELLING CALCULATION (PMC)

PMC does calculations on IFC models before the modelling is
completely finished, to ease the awkward phase where engineers
have to work with whatever the architect has made so far.

Simple calculations on easy points, using standard values from
EN/ISO standards and the Danish building regulations (BR18).

Daylight check (BR18 §379, the "10% rule"):
Occupied rooms (offices, classrooms, living rooms etc.) need a
window area of at least 10% of the room's floor area, unless
that light is coming only from skylights, in which case 7% is
enough. Bathrooms, storage, technical rooms, stairs and
corridors are exempt. This tool uses the geometry of each room
and window to work out the real ratio - not just what's written
in the model's own properties - and flags anything under the
threshold.

The 10% rule is a simplified check. BR18 also allows proving
daylight access via a daylight factor of 2% over half the room,
or 300 lux across half the floor area for half the daylight
hours - this tool does not attempt that calculation.

Features:
- Window-to-floor ratio per room, grouped by storey
- BR18 10% rule compliance check (threshold adjustable)
- CSV export

(c) 2026"""

